    "content": "Somalia's naval commander, Admiral Abdiwahhab Abdullahi Omar, participated in the 15th International Naval Power Symposium held in Venice, Italy, from October 6 to 8, 2026. The event, hosted at the Italian Navy's Arsenal headquarters, brought together naval leaders from various countries to discuss strategies for strengthening global maritime security.\n\nDuring the symposium, delegates addressed key issues including the protection of undersea communication cables, the adoption of advanced naval technologies, and the importance of international collaboration among nations with significant maritime interests. The conference provided a platform for sharing best practices and coordinating efforts to combat maritime threats.\n\nSomalia's involvement in this global forum underscores its commitment to securing its territorial waters and contributing to regional stability. In recent years, Somalia has worked to rebuild its naval forces with support from international partners, aiming to curb piracy and illegal fishing that have long plagued its coastline.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this participation signals a positive step toward a more secure and prosperous Somalia. Many diaspora members have invested in maritime industries or have family members dependent on fishing and trade. Enhanced maritime security can lead to safer shipping routes, reduced piracy risks, and improved economic opportunities along Somalia's extensive coastline.\n\nThe symposium also highlighted the need for continued capacity building for Somalia's navy, which remains a work in progress. International cooperation, as demonstrated at this event, is vital for Somalia to fully assume responsibility for its maritime domain.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/08/soomaaliya-oo-xoojinaysa-iskaashiga-amniga-badaha-kuna-biirtay-laba-shabakad-oo-caalami-ah/",
